rce-backed cross-Skill links resolve through the shared Source mapping; targets keep their own versions. Excludes paths batches and refresh:true.","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Maximum number of lines to read","type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)","type":"number"},{"type":"null"}]},"path":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Local file path (relative or absolute), an issued skill:// or sr: ref, or a supplied Notion Skill page URL. Notion main reads inspect without adopting task instructions. Copy refs verbatim; never guess filesystem paths.","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"paths":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Copy complete resource refs verbatim from the selected Skill snapshot's resource directory. Every ref must identify a file in the same owner and snapshot. Reads all selected files in one operation without preparing the main body.","items":{"pattern":"^(?:sr:R[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}|skill:\\/\\/.+)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"refresh":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Use only for a user-requested current-version inspection; a successful complete read needs no follow-up refresh. Keeps the active selection unchanged. Only for a supplied Notion Skill ref in path; fixed resources and local files keep their versions.","type":"boolean"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["path","offset","limit","paths","from","budget","refresh"],"type":"object"},"strict":true,"type":"function"},{"description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\n\nCodemode: `tools.bash(args)` resolves to `{ output, truncated, full_output_path?, exit_code, wall_time_seconds }`.","name":"bash","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"co